id: false-courage
name: False Courage
uaType: technical
prerequisite: Personality Score of 4+
tpCost: 8
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerBaseTier: 4
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Combat Rolls 1(T) lower and Soak Value 2(T) higher, until the start of your next turn.
text: >
  False Courage: Putting on a facade of bravado that you absolutely do not feel, you prepare for danger.
  –Ability Type: Technical
  –Prerequisites: Personality Score of 4+
  –TP Cost: 8
  –KP Cost: 4(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: Free
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: Reduce your Combat Rolls by 1(T), but increase your Soak Value by 2(T) until the start of your next turn.

---

# The whole of it is a duration: the False Courage mark (conditions/false-courage-mark.dbu) carries both numbers, and a start
# edge lifts it as your next turn begins - Brace's clock.
#
# "Minions: Free." There are no Minions in this system; carried as printed, as the Brace and Soar files carry theirs.
[on used]
gain(false-courage-mark);
expires(false-courage-mark, start-of-next-turn);
